{"id": "EUVD-2026-108922", "enisaUuid": "0e5d77a5-cca1-3820-8a30-25471d44585a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmlxsw: spectrum_flower: Fix port range register leak in tmplt_create()\n\nmlxsw_sp_flower_tmplt_create() parses a flow_cls_offload template\ninto a stack-local struct mlxsw_sp_acl_rule_info purely to compute\nrulei.values.elusage. Parsing can acquire port range registers via\nmlxsw_sp_flower_parse_ports_range(), but since this rulei never goes\nthrough mlxsw_sp_acl_rulei_destroy(), those registers were never\nreleased, including through chain template deletion.\n\nFactor out of mlxsw_sp_acl_rulei_destroy() the code to actually\nrelease the necessary resources and call from\nmlxsw_sp_flower_tmplt_create() to plug the leak.\n\nThe issue was found during a review of Wentao Liang's patch referenced\nbelow.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41ad5bcf0219aaebf8ffb052c5e8177479330cde", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c8e934287debb29c6ded86b21e49fc72e186d15e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3938430f0237c59ca08d6a366e7657b2b7f8d0bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4eaf1285b5c1e42f80e47f9fe0d391e70418db02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ea07afb230f1342ab0f9365edd0aae137f425d3"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98948"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cce88c1-3601-3cb0-bfb5-51e8cf4f29e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "13146c5f-8f8a-33ce-8e32-4af7239f73c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "14d66f1c-2c73-33b8-97a6-09d4de45d94f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "1f21a0c0-a1ef-3b35-91de-fc4d0bbabe9c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "pat